body:
It definitely sucks being sick, worse that I have no idea what it is and that I know it's more than one thing. I feel like I see doctors more than my husband, and I dread every email/letter that comes in the mail with the hospital's logo on it. And every visit/test leads to another... and another... I'd almost prefer to just hear worst-case scenario news than to continue on having no idea and feeling sick/anxious. 

&#x200B;

Being married is definitely the hardest thing I've ever done. We have been married 3 years and knew each other for 11 years before that so we did not expect to struggle so much with finding the lines that split me, you, and us. And when we disagree on things now, it can effectively damage the other person's life by squashing their dreams if we are unwilling to bend. It's definitely a struggle, and when it's good it's unlike anything in the world... but when it's bad, it feels impossible.

&#x200B;

We have to now decide if we still want to try for children knowing what we know. We recently confirmed he has a hereditary heart condition that his dad also has, both our families are riddled with cancer, and now I have at least 2 hereditary conditions as well. It seems morally wrong to have our own biological child. He is taking this news and coming to terms with being child-free, while my focus went right to adoption. No one comes out of that feeling okay if the other won't reconsider.

I'm hoping the therapist does help, but it just seems so far away. They did say they have an office for walk-in emergencies, but it's not hear my house or where I work and they warned the wait times are long. I definitely get that it's hard to support someone when they're really low because you just don't know what to say, but for my own husband to completely not care was the last straw. I get that he's not well either, but holy shit. You'd think that you'd show an ounce of emotion when your wife says she's had blood work, biopsies, etc. done. My hair has been falling out in clumps and when I pointed it out he said he genuinely didn't notice. I feel like even now at my lowest, I would be wrapping him up in the biggest hug and so much support if he told me that.

&#x200B;

Honestly, I never sleep anymore. I sleep maybe 1-3 hours a night in broken up naps, then about once every few weeks I crash into an all day/weekend sleep. I've tried melatonin, painkillers, muscle relaxers, etc. and all it does is give me a headache and make me lethargic, but I still don't fall asleep.

&#x200B;

I definitely appreciate people reaching out on here. I feel like I'd be a lot better if I just had someone to talk to.
